# Git workflow

## Default

Git writes are **denied** unless the Owner explicitly authorizes them for the current task.

Do not change global Git or Cursor settings or account Attribution preferences automatically.

## Commit messages

- Professional, concise, technical. Conventional Commits where appropriate.
- Never append AI-assistant attribution trailers or marketing signatures.

Forbidden in commit messages (and equivalent variants):

```
Co-authored-by: Cursor
Co-authored-by: Cursor AI
Co-authored-by: AI
Co-authored-by: Claude
Made-with: Cursor
Made with Cursor
Generated by Cursor
Generated with AI
Assisted by Cursor
```

Do not falsify author/committer identity. Product references to Cursor ACP functionality are allowed when accurate.

Before finishing a commit, run `python3 scripts/check_git_metadata.py <msgfile>` (or rely on the local hook). If tooling injects trailers, rewrite the commit message without them before push. Do not use `--no-verify`.

## Pull requests

Preferred integration: **Create a merge commit** (no squash, no rebase).

PR body must include:

```
Merge strategy: Merge commit (no squash/rebase)
```

Forbidden in PR descriptions (outside fenced code examples):

```
Made with Cursor
Made with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)
Made-with: Cursor
Generated by Cursor
```

File-based PR workflow:

1. Write the body to a local Markdown file.
2. `python3 scripts/check_git_metadata.py --pr-body-file body.md`
3. `gh pr create ... --body-file body.md`
4. Fetch the published body and re-validate; if a footer was injected, replace via `gh api` / `gh pr edit` and verify again.

Do not auto-merge. Owner retains final merge authority.

When merging via CLI: `gh pr merge <N> --merge` (never `--squash` / `--rebase`).

## Local hooks

Owner activation (repository-local only):

```
git config --local core.hooksPath .githooks
git config --local --get core.hooksPath
```

The presence of `.githooks/commit-msg` does not mean hooks are active until `core.hooksPath` is set.

## GitHub Actions

Workflow `.github/workflows/git-metadata.yml` validates PR bodies and commit messages.
Owner should mark it as a required status check to block merge when it fails.
